<item><title>South Africa mourns former deputy president Phumzile Mlambo-Ngcuka</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-africa-mourns-former-deputy-president-phumzile-mlambo-7199b5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-africa-mourns-former-deputy-president-phumzile-mlambo-7199b5/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>The country’s first female deputy president died on Friday at 71; the University of Johannesburg and political leaders paid tribute.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:11:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" length="36666" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
